    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "Prostaglandin (PG) levels in plasma and peritoneal fluid were determined in 10 sterilized women with pelvic pain without pathological findings. Another 15 women who were healthy were regarded as controls. The 6-keto-PGF(1alpha) levels in peritoneal fluid collected from patients with pelvic pain were significantly higher than that from controls (p 0.05. The results indicated that PGs might play an important role in pelvic pain following sterilization."
    }
